      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$u=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $Pu.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Pu=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Pu & =\\begin{bmatrix}m & n & -m \\\\ m & -n & -m \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ p \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}m\\cdot 1+n\\cdot p+(-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ m\\cdot 1+(-n)\\cdot p+(-m)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot p+0\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}m+np-m \\\\ m-np-m \\\\ 0+2p+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}np \\\\ -np \\\\ 2p\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
